      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Faulkton%2C_South_Dakota"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The community of Faulkton was founded in 1882, before South Dakota officially became a state.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.faulktonsd.com/city"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Faulkton became the county seat in 1886 after the railroad bypassed the original county seat of LaFoon.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.faulktonsd.com/city"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Farmers in the Faulkton area grow a wide range of crops, including soybeans, corn, rye, and sunflowers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
